# Revising against feedback (surgical modification)

* **Every subcomponent the feedback doesn't mention must round-trip
  unchanged** — same alias, same `<name>`, same content. Preserve
  `<public-surface>` signatures verbatim unless the feedback names them
  directly: screen collections consume this handle, and rewording it
  forces every consumer to revalidate.
* **"Rename X to Y"** — edit the `<name>` only. **"Add a
  subcomponent"** — add it without touching siblings. **"Drop
  subcomponent X"** — remove it, drop `<sub-dependencies>` edges
  touching it. **"Re-articulate the pubapi / privapi / failure-surface
  / policies section"** — edit only that section.
* Don't reshuffle `<primitives>` the feedback isn't pointed at; don't
  add "while we're here" tweaks.
